{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In 2016 Congress enacted PROMESA to address Puerto Rico\u2019s fiscal crisis."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Centro de Periodismo Investigativo (CPI) sued the Oversight Board in the U.S. District Court for Puerto Rico after its requests for public records were denied."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The legal question was whether PROMESA contains a clear statement that actions against the Oversight Board may be brought in federal court, thereby waiving the Board\u2019s sovereign immunity."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2022-22-96",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that PROMESA does not contain the unmistakable language required to abrogate the Oversight Board\u2019s sovereign immunity."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Because the statute lacks a categorical abrogation, PROMESA\u2019s judicial\u2011review scheme remains in place but does not waive immunity."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In dissent, the United States argued that Puerto Rico should be allowed to invoke a form of common\u2011law immunity in federal court."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Decision",
    "status": "complete",
