              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case concerned whether the Puerto Rico Oversight, Management, and Economic Stability Act (PROMESA) waives sovereign immunity of the Financial Oversight and Management Board, allowing lawsuits in federal court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that Congress did not use the unmistakable language required to abrogate sovereign immunity, so the Board retains its immunity."
      }
    ],
